# Build context for docker/Dockerfile, which does `COPY . .` from the repo
# root. Without this file that copy sweeps in the real .env — SECRET_KEY and
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN included — and bakes it into an image layer, where it
# stays readable to anyone who can pull the image even though compose
# supplies those same values at runtime via env_file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The frontend has its own image built from its own context (./frontend), so
# none of it belongs in the backend image. This is also the single biggest
# win here: node_modules alone dwarfs everything the backend actually ships.
frontend/

# History, not code. Also carries every past value of every file, which is
# the last thing that should travel inside a runtime image.
.git/
.github/

# Local tooling state — all of it regenerated on demand, none of it valid
# inside the image anyway (a host .venv is built against the host's Python).
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Editor and OS noise.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Private planning docs — gitignored, and equally out of place in an image.
ARCHITECTURE.md
docs/
